summary:
  The writer's guard is started with the stream's pipe as its input.

history:
  The guard is born inside the pipe that carries the stream. Holding
  that pipe open, it kept curl from ever seeing that the writer had gone:
  measured, curl and the run's shell outlived a stop until the guard's next
  look, up to five seconds on.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SlideLogic.js

find:
  "bash " + q(a.guardPath) + " watch \"$$\" \"$PPID\" \"$fp\" </dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1 3<&- & "

replace:
  "bash " + q(a.guardPath) + " watch \"$$\" \"$PPID\" \"$fp\" >/dev/null 2>&1 3<&- & "

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_slidelogic.qml::test_the_writer_looks_before_it_cuts_and_never_names_the_address.
